/-!
# Native M22 involution and odd-prime displacement

The odd-prime displacement bound six and an attaining cubic element are
proved for the actual ten-dimensional code and cocode, including their
setwise-pair extensions. The equality criterion uses actual native fixed
points. Native involutions have displacement four. In the setwise-pair
extension, fixed-point-free involutions have displacement five, while outer
involutions with fixed points have displacement three. These ranks follow
from the ambient cocode calculations, the proved marked-pair incidence test,
and rank-nullity for the actual pair-line quotient.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, H.13 parameter discussion and H.14.4, printed
pp.395--398, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004.
-/
